	'ou_s0h'             => 'A Former Print Shop in Ghent',
	'ou_s0b'             => 'Yoru Bar opened in 2017 at Maanstraat 7 in Ghent, occupying the subterranean basement where a letterpress print shop once operated. When founder Margit Vos first descended the worn stone steps, the room held thick brick arches, cool air, and a secluded silence beneath the city streets. Rather than opening the space into a crowded hall, we chose to preserve that quiet seclusion. We installed a single solid walnut counter curving beneath ink-blue tiled walls, illuminated only by small brass lamps, creating an intimate refuge for conversation and considered drinks.',
	'ou_s1h'             => 'Why Twelve Seats and Three Seatings?',
	'ou_s1b'             => 'Twelve seats represent the exact number of guests two bartenders can attend to without haste or compromise. With seats one through eight facing the bartender and nine through twelve at the window end, every guest has a direct view of the mixing glasses, the jiggers, and the ice. By dividing our open hours from 19:00 to 01:00 into three two-hour seatings, we give each group the time and space to settle in, explore the list, and experience the room without standing crowds waiting behind their stools.',
	'ou_s2h'             => 'Why is Yoru Bar reservation only?',
